+# What is finished, what is not, and what the rest needs
+
+This document exists because "is it done" deserves a real answer rather than a
+version number. The product's own rule is that a thing claims only what it has
+proven; the same rule applies to the project.
+
+Read the middle column as strictly as the status badges in the interface.
+
+---
+
+## The decision layer — finished
+
+Everything here is portable C++20 with no Windows, no GPU and no SDK. It builds
+and runs anywhere, and 276 assertions run against it in about a second.
+
+| Area | State |
+|---|---|
+| Capability graph, evidence ledger, TTL decay | **Done.** Nothing can reach ACTIVE without fresh liveness. |
+| Intent → Planner → Plan, pure and total | **Done.** |
+| Look model, strength response curves | **Done.** |
+| Temporal arbitration, motion source rules | **Done.** |
+| Camera discovery, matrix inversion, reprojection | **Done**, tested against synthetic drives with decoy matrices. |
+| Budget governor, degrade ladder, latency model | **Done.** |
+| Pass model — the 1.00–2.00 dial, split solving, half-res delta | **Done.** |
+| Video memory accounting | **Done.** |
+| Per-material model — `semantic.hpp` | **Done.** |
+| Backend contract — `backend.hpp` | **Done.** |
+| Draw classification and frame segmentation | **Done.** |
+| Overlay coverage model | **Done.** |
+| Material catalogue and its file format | **Done.** |
+
+| Recorded decisions across a grid of situations | **Done.** |
+
+This half is genuinely finished in the sense that matters: it is the part where
+being wrong is silent, and it is the part that is checked.
+
+`tests/golden/plans.txt` holds the whole decision for ten situations - a fresh
+install, the tuned personal setup, a second pass with and without a capable
+provider, skin identified, the governor under load, safe mode, frames refused
+for want of motion. Change a rule and the diff names which situations moved.
+That is either the change that was intended, in which case the recording is
+updated deliberately with `EMKO_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1`, or it is the one that was not.
+
+This matters more from here than it did before: the next phase is *run it, find
+things, change code*, and that is exactly the phase where a threshold moved for
+one reason quietly changes what happens in a case nobody was looking at.
+
+---
+
+## The Windows layer — partly built, none of it run
+
+Everything below compiles only on Windows against the ReShade, RenoDX and
+Windows SDKs. **None of it has been executed.** It is type-checked against stub
+headers, which catches wrong names and wrong signatures and catches nothing
+else. A stub is written from the same understanding as the code it checks, so
+where that understanding is wrong, both are wrong together — which is exactly
+what a first run on a real machine is for.
+
+| Area | State |
+|---|---|
+| Add-on lifecycle, ReShade registration | Written, unrun |
+| Telemetry block, config store, journal | Written, unrun |
+| Probes and effectors | Written, unrun |
